For the method calls<pre>init(opmode, key);
init(opmode, key, paramSpec);
init(opmode, key, params);
init(opmode, key, paramSpec, secureRandom);
init(opmode, key, params, secureRandom);
init(opmode, key, secureRandom);</pre>use different algorithms if <details><summary>key is a <code>javax.crypto.SecretKey</code></summary>The algorithm has to be one of the following:<ul><li>AES</li> <li>PBEWithHmacSHA224AndAES_128</li> <li>PBEWithHmacSHA256AndAES_128</li> <li>PBEWithHmacSHA384AndAES_128</li> <li>PBEWithHmacSHA512AndAES_128</li> <li>PBEWithHmacSHA224AndAES_256</li> <li>PBEWithHmacSHA256AndAES_256</li> <li>PBEWithHmacSHA384AndAES_256</li> <li>PBEWithHmacSHA512AndAES_256</li></ul></details>or<details><summary>key is a <code>java.security.PublicKey</code> or <code>java.security.PrivateKey</code></summary>The algorithm has to be <i>RSA</i>.</details><br>For the following method calls<pre>init(opmode, certificate);
init(opmode, certificate, secureRandom);</pre>if a <code>java.security.Certificate</code> is used the algorithm has to be <i>RSA</i>.<br><br>For all mentioned method calls, if opmode is one of <code>WRAP_MODE</code> or <code>UNWRAP_MODE</code> the algorithm also has to be <i>RSA</i>.</details>
